@aiwayds/dsh-topics-memory README · Quick start：1. Install (command below), restart dsh;
2. Run `/topics onboard` — native dsh ask-user panels walk you through the five decisions: mode / repo / distill model / injection tier / auto-observe — nothing is written until the final confirm;
3. Work as usual: relevant conclusions are injected every turn; say "remember…" to have the model `topic_save`; `/topics status` for health, `/topics stats` for injection stats.

@aiwayds/dsh-topics-memory README · Uninstall：- `~/.dsh/topics/` — the whole topic bundle: topic markdown, `meta/`, and the embedded `.git` repo (the full history; it may carry an `origin` remote — GitHub sync stops with the plugin). To archive the bundle elsewhere, copy or clone this directory as-is.
- The settings-page `dsh-topics-memory` entry (profile patch) — user overrides. Reinstalling silently reactivates sync including any configured `repo`; clear the entry first if you want a clean start.
- A legacy `llmwiki:` section left inside the old `settings.yaml` (renamed `settings.yaml.imported` after the host's one-shot 0.1.7 import) is never touched again; mine it by hand if something still needs it.
